���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� ���������������� �������� ������������������ ������ �������������������� �������������� ������������ ������ ���������������� ������ �������� �������������� ��������������������������\n������������������������ ������ �������� �������������������������� ���������� ������ �������� �������������������� ������ ���� ���������������������� ������������������ ��������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_277": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \n  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 277 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n  \nSWADESH DARSHAN SCHEME \n  \n277.  SHRI MALOOK NAGAR: \n           SHRI RAMSHIROMANI VERMA: \n  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the name of the historical cities/places which are \nproposed to be connected by trains under the Swadesh \nDarshan Scheme of the Government; \n(b) whether the Government proposes to connect the \nhistorical cities of Hastinapur and Shravasti with other \nmajor cities of the country through rail -links under the \nsaid scheme; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMERCE & INDUSTRY AND \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a):      Railways does not run trains under the Swadesh Darshan \nscheme of the Government.   However, Indian Railway Catering and \nTourism Corporation (IRCTC) is operating on multiple theme based \ncircuits across the country which connect historical cities/pl aces \nviz. Ayodhya, Varanasi, Ujjain, Agra, Prayagraj, Baidyanath, \nBodhgaya, Rajgir, Nalanda, Nagpur, Indore, Aurangabad, Chitrakoot, \nMathura, Vrindavan, Puri,  Gangasagar, Tirupati, Madurai, \nRameshwaram, Srirangapatnam, Mysore, Dwarka, Ankaleshwar, \nNasik, Jaisalmer, Jodhpur, Bikaner, Jaipur, Udaipur, Ajmer, \nKhajuraho, Orchha, Sarnath, Kushinagar, Sravasti, Fatehpur Sikri, \nNathdwara, Nandigram, Sitamadhi, Hampi, Mumbai, Gokarana, \nBelur, Jabalpur, Coorg, Thanjavur. \n \n(b) & (c):         Do not arise. \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_278": "1 \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LAW AND JUSTICE \nDEPARTMENT OF JUSTICE \n****** \nLOK   SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 278 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 3-2- 2021 \n \nFast Track Courts  \n \n278.  SHRIMATI  VEENA DEVI:  \n \nWill the Minister of LAW AND JUSTICE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether fast track courts have been established in Bihar; \n(b) if so, the details thereof;   \n(c)whether the required funds are not being released for smooth operation \nof the fast track courts and the reaction of Government thereto; and  \n(d) if so, the details of funds released to Bihar for the above mentioned task \nduring the last four years? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF LAW & JUSTICE, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI RAVI SHANKAR PRASAD) \n(a) to(d):Setting up of Fast Track Court s (FTCs) and its functioning falls  \nwithin the domain of the State Governments in consultation with the \nrespective High Courts. As per information obtained from the  Patna High \nCourt, at present ,33 FTCs are functional in the State of Bihar . The \n\n2 \n \n14thFinance Co mmission had urged all State Governments to utilize the \nenhanced fiscal space available through tax devolution (32% to 42%) to \nmeet the financial requirement of the FTCs. The details of funds \nreleasedby Bihar during the last 4 years for FTCs are as under: \n \n**** \nFinancial \nYear \nFunds allocated by the \nState Government                                                                                       \n( inRs. Cr.) \nFunds released \n( inRs.Cr.) \n2016-17 67.686 0 \n2017-18 67.0437 17.66 \n2018-19 67.686 18.50 \n2019-20 40.00 11.56 ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_279": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. † *279 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 15.03.2021 \n \nVOCATIONAL TRAINING CENTRES IN MAHARASHTRA \n \n†*279. SHRI PRATAPRAO JADHAV : \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be \npleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has implemented any sche me to set up vocational training \ncentres to provide alternative employment to the un employed persons in the country, \nparticularly in the backward and rural regions of Maharashtra;  \n(b) if so, the State-wise details thereof, particul arly in the backward and rural regions of \nMaharashtra;  \n(c) whether the Government proposes to open more su ch training centres in the country, \nparticularly in the backward and rural regions of Maharashtra during the current year; and  \n(d) if so, the details thereof?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER IN THE MINISTRY OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(DR. MAHENDRA NATH PANDEY) \n \n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the  House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) of LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. †*279 TO BE ANSWERED ON 15.03.2021 RAI SED BY SHRI \nPRATAPRAO JADHAV REGARDING ‘VOCATIONAL TRAINING CEN TRES IN \nMAHARASHTRA’ \n \n(a) to  (d):  The Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepreneur ship (MSDE) is \nimplementing several schemes for imparting employab le skills through short-duration and \nlong-duration skill training. The details of vocati onal training centres in these schemes are \ngiven below: \n \n(1) MSDE is implementing the flagship scheme, Pradh an \nMantriKaushalVikasYojana(PMKVY), under which short- duration training is provided through \nthree routes, namely Short-Term Training (STT) for freshskilling of school / college drop outs \nand unemployed youth; Recognition of Prior Learning  (RPL) to recognize the existingskills \nthrough orientation; and Special Projects to addres s skilling requirements of the vulnerable \ngroups. Training under PMKVY is provided through em panelledTraining Providers / Centres . \nThe State / Union Territory (UT ) - wise number of empanelledTraining Centres under PMK VY \n2.0 (2016 -2020 ), as of 19 .01 .2021, is given at Annexure-I. \n \nMSDE has also taken the initiative to create Pradha n MantriKaushalKendras (PMKKs ) as \nvisible and aspirational model training centres in every district of India. As of 19 .01 .2021, 738 \nPMKKs have been established. The State/ UT - wise n umber of PMKKs set up (as of \n19.01.2021) are given at Annexure-II . \n \n(2) Under the scheme, Jan ShikshanSansthan (JSS ), skill training is imparted to the socio -\neconomically backward and educationally disadvantag ed groups of urban / rural population \nsuch as neo -literates, semi -literates, Scheduled Castes, Scheduled Tribes, wome n and girls, \nslum dwellers, migrant workers, etc . The number of districts of sanctioned JSS, State / UT – \nwise, is given at Annexure-III. \n \n(3) Under Craftsmen Training Scheme, long-duration skill training is imparted through \nIndustrial Training Institutes (ITIs) in 137 trades . The State/ UT – wise number of ITIs is given \nat Annexure-IV .  \n \nIn addition, the Government has approved the settin g up of Indian Institute of Skills (IISs) in \nPublic Private Partnership (PPP) mode in three loca tions in the country namely Mumbai, \nKanpur and Ahmedabad. The first batch at IIS Mumbai  has commenced training in December \n2020.  \n  \n\nAnnexure I  \n \nAnnexure-I referred to in reply to LS SQ No. †*279 to be answered on 15.03.2021 \nregarding ‘VOCATIONAL TRAINING CENTRES IN MAHARASHTRA’ \n \nState/ UT - wise number of empanelled Training Cent res(TCs) under PMKVY 2.0 (2016-\n2020) (as of 19.01.2021) \n \nSl . \nNo. \nState / UT  No . of empanelled TCs  \n1. Andaman and Nicobar Islands 8 \n2. Andhra Pradesh 471 \n3. Arunachal Pradesh 92 \n4. Assam 335 \n5. Bihar 454 \n6. Chandigarh 55 \n7. Chhattisgarh 166 \n8. Dadra and Nagar Haveli 6 \n9. Daman and Diu 12 \n10. Delhi 376 \n11. Goa 24 \n12. Gujarat 414 \n13. Haryana 1,045 \n14. Himachal Pradesh 307 \n15. Jammu and Kashmir 355 \n16. Jharkhand 210 \n17. Karnataka 273 \n18. Kerala 322 \n19. Lakshadweep 1 \n20. Madhya Pradesh 1,079 \n21 . Maharashtra  794  \n22. Manipur 113 \n23. Meghalaya 71 \n24. Mizoram 72 \n25. Nagaland 69 \n26. Odisha 376 \n27. Puducherry 40 \n28. Punjab 794 \n29. Rajasthan 1,384 \n30. Sikkim 31 \n31. Tamil Nadu 1,069 \n32. Telangana 469 \n33. Tripura 147 \n34. Uttar Pradesh 2,091 \n35. Uttarakhand 372 \n36. West Bengal 456 \n Total  14,353  \n\nAnnexure II  \n \nAnnexure-II referred to in reply to LS SQ No. †*279  to be answered on 15.03.2021 \nregarding ‘VOCATIONAL TRAINING CENTRES IN MAHARASHTRA’ \n \nState/ UT - wise number of PMKKs set up (as of 19.01.2021) \n \nState / UT  No . of Districts in the State  No . of PMKKs established  \nAndaman and Nicobar \nIslands \n3 1 \nAndhra Pradesh 13 24 \nArunachal Pradesh 25 8 \nAssam 33 29 \nBihar 38 48 \nChandigarh 1 1 \nChhattisgarh 28 27 \nDelhi 11 10 \nGoa 2 1 \nGujarat 33 34 \nHaryana 22 23 \nHimachal Pradesh 12 11 \nJammu and Kashmir 20 19 \nJharkhand 24 24 \nKarnataka 30 35 \nKerala 14 19 \nLadakh 2 1 \nLakshadweep 1 0 \nMadhya Pradesh 52 52 \nMaharashtra  36  43  \nManipur 16 13 \nMeghalaya 11 4 \nMizoram 11 2 \nNagaland 11 3 \nOdisha 30 29 \nPuducherry 4 4 \nPunjab 22 24 \nRajasthan 33 35 \nSikkim 4 2 \nTamil Nadu 37 34 \nTelangana 33 28 \nDadra & Nagar Haveli and \nDaman & Diu \n3 2 \nTripura 8 4 \nUttar Pradesh 75 87 \nUttarakhand 13 13 \nWest Bengal 23 44 \nTotal  734  738  \nNote : Includes PMKKs which were later surrendered / de -allocated by training partners, \nlocations rolled back . \n\n \nAnnexure III  \n \nAnnexure-III referred to in reply to LS SQ No. †*27 9 to be answered on 15.03.2021 \nregarding ‘VOCATIONAL TRAINING CENTRES IN MAHARASHTRA’ \n \nState/ UT - wise number of sanctioned Jan ShikshanSansthans \n \nState / UT  No . of d istrict s of sanctioned JSS  \nAndhra Pradesh 7 \nArunachal Pradesh 1 \nAssam 5 \nBihar 13 \nChandigarh 1 \nChhattisgarh 7 \nDadra & Nagar Haveli 1 \nDelhi 3 \nGoa 1 \nGujarat 11 \nHaryana 5 \nHimachal Pradesh 1 \nJammu & Kashmir 2 \nJharkhand 4 \nKarnataka  9 \nKerala 9 \nMadhya Pradesh 33 \nMaharashtra  21  \nManipur 3 \nNagaland  1 \nOdisha 17 \nPunjab 2 \nRajasthan  7 \nTamil Nadu 9 \nTelangana  7 \nTripura 1 \nUttar Pradesh 53 \nUttarakhand 6 \nWest Bengal  8 \nTotal  248  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure IV  \n \nAnnexure-IV referred to in reply to LS SQ No. †*279  to be answered on 15.03.2021 \nregarding ‘VOCATIONAL TRAINING CENTRES IN MAHARASHTRA’ \n \nState/ UT – wise number of ITIs count as on 10.03.2 021 \n \nSl . No . State /UT  No . of ITIs  \n1. Andaman & Nicobar Islands 4 \n2. Andhra Pradesh 510 \n3. Arunachal Pradesh 5 \n4. Assam 36 \n5 Bihar 1,246 \n6. Chandigarh 2 \n7. Chhattisgarh 228 \n8. Dadra and Nagar Haveli and  1 \n9. Daman and Diu 2 \n10. Delhi 52 \n11. Goa 13 \n12. Gujarat 500 \n13. Haryana 397 \n14. Himachal Pradesh 268 \n15. Jammu and Kashmir 50 \n16. Jharkhand 323 \n17. Karnataka 1,498 \n18. Kerala 462 \n19. Lakshadweep 1 \n20. Madhya Pradesh 1,067 \n21. Maharashtra  1,000  \n22. Manipur 1 \n23. Meghalaya 6 \n24. Mizoram 3 \n25. Nagaland 8 \n26. Odisha 502 \n27. Puducherry 14 \n28. Punjab 352 \n29. Rajasthan 1,791 \n30. Sikkim 3 \n31. Tamil Nadu 494 \n32. Telangana 291 \n33. Tripura 21 \n34. Uttar Pradesh 3,207 \n35. Uttarakhand 189 \n36. West Bengal 266 \nTotal  14,813  \n \n**** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_280": " \n \n������������������� �\n��������������������� �\n����������������������������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n�������������������� �����\n������������������ �����������\n�\n��������������� �\n�\n������� ������������������������� �\n������������������������������ �\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� ��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� ������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� �������� ��� ����� ����� ������ ��� ������ ������������ ����������� ���� ������������ ����\n�������������������������������������������������\n�\n���� ���������������������������������\n�\n���� ������������������������������\n�\n������ �\n������������ ��������� �\n�������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������\n�\n�\n������ �\n\n \n \n��������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� ��������� � ������ ���� ������� ��� ����������� ������ ��� �����\n����� ���������� ���� ���� ����� ��������� ������ ��������� �����������������\n��������������������������������������� �\n�\n������������� ���������� ��� �� �������� ��� ���� ����������� ����� ��� ���� �����������������\n��������� ��� �������� ���� ������ ���� ������������� ��� ���� ������ ������������� � ������ ����\n�������� ��������� ��� �������� ��� ����� ��� �������� �������������� ��� ������ ��� ������ ����\n������������������������������������������������\n�\n� ���� �������� ����������� ���� ����� �� ��������� ������� ���� ���� ����\n�������������������������������