    "ls|LS17_S5_U_334": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.334\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021\nVANDE BHARAT MISSION\n334.    SHRI BHOLANATH (B.P . SAROJ):\nWill the Minister of External Affairs be pleased to state:\n(a) the details of number of persons brought to India under the Vande\nBharat Mission in its various phases along with details, country-wise;\n(b) the  manner  in  which  these  passengers  were  screened  and\nquarantined;\n(c) the total number of neighboring countries that sought the help of\nIndia for purchase of COVID-19 vaccines from India, country-wise\nand quantity of vaccines sought by them;\n(d) whether some of these countries are likely to be provided these\nvaccines as gift; and\n(e) if so, the details thereof?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[SHRI V. MURALEEDHARAN]\n(a)  As per the information available with Ministry of External Affairs, as on\n20 January 2021, around 39 lakh people have returned to India under 9\nphases of the Vande Bharat Mission. Since most Indian nationals stranded in\nforeign  countries  have  safely  returned  to  their  homes,  the  incoming\npassengers are now being treated as ‘International Arrivals’. A country-wise\nlist is attached at Annexure A.\n(b) Ministry of Health & Family Welfare and Ministry of Home Affairs\nhave been issuing revised guidelines on screening and quarantine from\ntime to time. Based on these guidelines, State Governments have been\nissuing  their  own  SOPs  for  arriving  passengers  for  the  purpose  of\nscreening, testing and quarantine.\n(c) to (e) As on 22 January 2021, India has provided Covid-19 vaccines in\nform of grant-in-aid to following countries:\n Sl. \nNo. Countries Doses\n1 Bhutan 1.5 lakh\n2 Maldives 1 lakh\n3 Bangladesh 20 lakh\n4 Nepal 10 lakh\n5 Myanmar 15 lakh\n1\n\n6 Mauritius 1 lakh\n7 Seychelles 50,000\n2\n\nAnnexure- I to Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 334\nCountry wise Number of Repatriated Indians upto 20.01.2021\nCOUNTRY WISE NUMBER OF REPATRIATED INDIANS TILL\n20.01.2021\nCOUNTRY NO. OF REPATRIATED INDIANS\nAFGHANISTAN 15603\nALGERIA 1338\nANGOLA 770\nARMENIA 720\nAUSTRALIA 12593\nAZERBAIJAN 186\nBAHRAIN 56532\nBANGLADESH 26560\nBARBADOS 115\nBELARUS 232\nBELGIUM 296\nBHUTAN 1801\nBRAZIL 510\nBRUNEI 408\nBULGARIA 698\nCAMBODIA 596\nCANADA 61504\nCHINA 1257\nCROATIA 3\nDENMARK 52\nDJIBOUTI 326\nEGYPT 1892\nESTONIA 6\nETHIOPIA 11274\nFIJI 5\nFINLAND 223\nFRANCE 54246\nGEORGIA 2047\nGERMANY 65260\nGHANA 302\nGREECE 163\nHONG KONG 2248\nHUNGARY 3\nINDONESIA 4026\nIRAN 5332\nIRAQ 12412\nIRELAND 485\nISRAEL 1105\nITALY 9647\nJAPAN 9290\nJORDAN 838\nKAZAKHSTAN 3686\n3\n\nKENYA 7922\nKUWAIT 170595\nKYRGYZSTAN 11297\nLAOS 427\nLATVIA 5\nLEBANON 893\nMADAGASCAR 84\nMALAYSIA 32313\nMALDIVES 52248\nMALI 237\nMALTA 256\nMAURITIUS 1582\nMEXICO 228\nMOLDOVA 243\nMONGOLIA 34\nMOROCCO 99\nMYANMAR 1635\nNEPAL 6147\nNETHERLANDS 17921\nNEW ZEALAND 1897\nNIGERIA 6233\nNORWAY 267\nOMAN 216910\nOTHERS 11515\nPAKISTAN 683\nPHILIPPINES 8473\nPOLAND 342\nPORTUGAL 54\nQATAR 226660\nROMANIA 8\nRUSSIA 10923\nRWANDA 1124\nSAUDI ARABIA 365929\nSCOTLAND 35\nSEYCHELLES 2343\nSINGAPORE 63691\nSOUTH AFRICA 1161\nSOUTH KOREA 3484\nSPAIN 1117\nSRI LANKA 16667\nSUDAN 125\nSWEDEN 1270\nSWITZERLAND 27\nSYRIA 12\nTAIWAN 144\nTAJIKISTAN 2085\nTANZANIA 5435\nTHAILAND 4700\nTUNISIA 25\n4\n\nTURKEY 2156\nTURKMENISTAN 105\nUNITED ARAB EMIRATES 1568469\nUNITED KINGDOM 152913\nUKRAINE 8622\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA 250937\nUZBEKISTAN 1937\nVIETNAM 1387\nYEMEN 184\nZIMBABWE 5\nTOTAL BY AIR 3610810\nTOTAL BY SEA 3987\nTOTAL BY LAND 397106\n***\n5",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_335": " \n \n1 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS  \nDEPARTMENT OF POSTS \n \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 335  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 3RD FEBRUARY, 2021 \n \nNEW POST OFFICES IN TAMIL NADU \n \n335. DR. A. CHALLAKUMAR:  \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  the number and details of new post offices opened/made functional in the State of Tamil \nNadu during the last five years; and  \n \n(b)  the number of new post offices out of these made functional in Krishnagiri district of \nTamil Nadu? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR COMMUNICATIONS, EDUCATION AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY  \n(SHRI SANJAY DHOTRE) \n \n(a)   Sir, there are 32 new post offices, comprising of 17 Sub Post Offices and 15 Branch Post \nOffices opened/ made functional in the State Tamil Nadu during the last five years as per the \ndetails in Annexure-I & II respectively. \n(b)  Out of these,  one new post office namely Kumudepalli Sub Post office was made \nfunctional in Krishnagiri district of Tamil Nadu in the year 2015-16. \n  \n  \n\n \n \n2 \n \n \n \nAnnexure- I \nAnnexure referred to in reply of para  (a) of Lok Sabha Unstarred question No.335 to be answered \non 03.02.2021 raised by Hon’ble Member of Parliament Dr. A. Challakumar, regarding “New Post \nOffices in Tamil Nadu”. \n \nDetails of new Sub Post Offices opened/ made functional during the last five \nyears \nSl. No Name of Sub Post \nOffices \nDistrict Year \n1 Ulkottai \n \nAriyalur 2015-16 \n2 Padur Kanchipuram \n3 Allikuttai Salem \n4 Kumudepalli Krishnagiri \n5 Karuthapulianpatti Madurai \n6 Athipatti Virudhunagar \n7 Sirupakkam Villupuram \n8 Central University of \nTamilnadu Campus \nTiruvarur 2016-17 \n9 Thirumudivakkam Kanchipuram \n10 Neelankarai Chennai \n11 Tiruppur Collectorate Tiruppur \n12 Namakal Dist court Namakkal 2017-18 \n13 Sithalapakkam Kanchipuram \n14 Tamilnadu national Law \nschool \nTrichy \n15 Solakadu Namakkal \n16 Devala Nilgiris 2018-19 \n17 Reddipalayam Ariyalur \n \n \n  \n \n \n \n\n \n \n3 \n \n \n \n \nAnnexure- II \nAnnexure referred to in reply of para (a) of Lok Sabha Unstarred question No.335 to be answered \non 03.02.2021 raised by Hon’ble Member of Parliament Dr. A. Challakumar, regarding “New Post \nOffices in Tamil Nadu”. \nDetails of new Branch Post Offices opened/ made functional during the last five \nyears \nSl. No Name of Branch \nPost Offices \nDistrict Year \n1 Oraikkalpalayam Coimbatore 2015-16 \n2 Andavarkovil Karur \n3 Mudalaipatti Trichy \n4 Seyed Ammal \nEngineering \nRamanathapuram \n5 Chitravadi Kanchipuram 2016-17 \n6 Sembarai Trichy \n7 Melakrishnaperi Tirunelveli \n8 Gudry Erode \n9 Thangappapuram Kanchipuram 2017-18 \n10 Ponnavarai Thanjavur \n11 Nachipatti Namakkal \n12 Saminattham Virudhunagar \n13 Suthamalli vilaku Tirunelveli \n14 Adhanur Kanchipuram 2018-19 \n15 Ottiambakkam Kanchipuram \n \n \n \n************ ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_336": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF POWER \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.336 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.03.2021 \n \nDAMAGE OF CROPS AT NTPC KAHALGAON \n \n†*336. SHRI AJAY KUMAR MANDAL: \n \nWill the Minister of POWER \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether due to damage of embankment of  Lagoon-3D in NTPC, \nKahalgaon during the year 2020, crops of thousands of farmers got damaged \nby ash mixed water in their farms; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)  whether any compensation has been paid to the affected farmers and if \nso, the details thereof; \n \n(d)  the number of displaced persons due to the setting  up of this \nplant/power station who have been given  employment in skilled/unskilled \ncategory; and \n \n(e)  the number of villages adopted by NTPC,  Kahalgaon so far including \nthe extent of development therein? \n \nA N S W E R \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR POWER, NEW & \nRENEWABLE ENERGY AND THE MINISTER OF STATE FOR SKILL \nDEVELOPMENT & ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \n(SHRI  R.K. SINGH)  \n \n \n(a) to (e) : A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n******* \n  \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( e) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 336 TO BE ANSWERED IN THE LOK SABHA ON  18.03.2021 \nREGARDING DAMAGE OF CROPS AT NTPC KAHALGAON. \n********* \n \n(a) to (c) :  There was a breach in Lagoon -3D embankment of NTPC \nKahalgaon in the month of November, 2020. On account of spillage of ash \nmixed water, crops of Mauja of Ekchari, Rasalpur, Maheshamunda and \nDhanaura of Bhagalpur District of Bihar have been affected. Government of \nBihar has constituted a Committee to examine the extent of damage of crops \nand the compensation would be paid in accordance with findings of the \nCommittee.  \n \n(d) & (e) : Fifteen (15) numbers of land oustees have been given permanent \nemployment in skilled category in last five years.  The commun ity \ndevelopmental works undertaken by NTPC -Kahalgaon are primarily in the \nareas of education, health, sanitation, drinking water, rural social \ninfrastructure, skill development, support to physically challenged, \nenvironmental sustainability and augmenting Government efforts and \nschemes for inclusive growth. These initiatives are based on the needs of the \ncommunity and availability of budget/resources thereof.  \n \n \n********** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_337": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *337 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.03.2021 \n \nSports Infrastructure in Assam \n \n*337. SHRI PRADYUT BORDOLOI: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the funds allocated to the State of Assam for enhancement of basic \ninfrastructure of playgrounds, stadiums and other sports -related \ninfrastructure during the last three years; \n \n(b) the details of the projects sanctioned and the funds released during \nthe said period for the State of Assam, district-wise; \n \n(c) whether new sports complexes have been constructed in the North \nEastern States during the last three years; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof along with the expenditure involved , State-\nwise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS & SPORTS  \n{ SHRI KIREN RIJIJU } \n \n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_338": "������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n������������������������������ �\n��������� �\n������������������������� �\n������������������� ������������������\n�\n���� �������������������������������� �\n����������������������������� �\n����������������������������������������\n���������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������ ����������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������� �\n��������������������������������\n�\n�\n���������������������������\n�\n����������������� � � � � � ������������������� �\n����������������������������� �\n�\n�\n������ ������������� ����� ��� ���������� ��� ���� �������� ������������ ������ ���� �������� ���� ����\n�������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������\n� ����� ������� ��� ����� ��������� �� ��������� ���� ��������� ��� ������ ��� ��������� ����\n������� ������� ��� ������� ���������� � ������ ��� ������ ��� ���������� ������������ ��� ���� ������ ���\n������������� ���� ��������������� ������������� ���� ������������������� ������ ���������� ���������\n���������� ������������������ ��������� �������� ����� ���� ���������� ��� ����������������� ����������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������"