    "ls|LS17_S5_U_358": "  \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 358 \nANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nNATIONAL MINERAL EXPLORATION TRUST \n358. SHRI RITESH PANDEY \nWill the Minister of MINES be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government established a PPP model 'National Mineral  \nExploration Trust' (NMET) to encourage private sector participation and  for giving a \nfillip to mineral exploration in the country; \n(b) the number of private exploration agencies empanelled for the  NMET till date; \nand \n(c) the number of projects approved for NMET along with the  details of the Mineral -\nwise  and  State- wise  distributions  of  mineral exploration  projects  approved \nunder the aforesaid project till date? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF MINES, COAL AND PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI) \n \n(a) The Government has established  National Minerals Exploration Trust (NMET) for \ngiving a fillip to mineral exploration in the country. It has not been established on a \nPPP model. \n \n(b) No private exploration agencies have empanelled for the NMET till date. \n \n(c) A total of 191 number of projects have been approved till date by NMET. Details \nof the mineral and state wise approved projects are given below; \ni. Mineral-wise distribution of mineral exploration projects approved till date; \nSl. No. Commodity No. of Projects \n1 Iron Ore 18 \n2 Limestone 77 \n3 Manganese 18 \n4 Bauxite 16 \n5 Copper 7 \n6 Gold 6 \n7 Gold and Basemetal 4 \n8 Basemetal 7 \n9 Copper and Gold 2 \n10 Fe-Ni-Cr 1 \n11 Tin 1 \n\n12 Coal/Lignite 4 \n13 PGE 1 \n14 Diamond 2 \n15 Andalusite 1 \n16 Fertilizer Minerals 4 \n17 Tungsten 1 \n18 Magnesite 1 \n19 Environmental Studies 1 \n20 Associated Minerals 5 \n21 Molybdenum 1 \n22 Baseline Geoscience Surveys 13 \n  Total 191 \n  \n(ii)  State-wise distribution of mineral exploration projects approved till date; \nS. No. Name of the State No. of Projects \n1 Andhra Pradesh 12 \n2 Chhattisgarh 18 \n3 Jharkhand 9 \n4 Karnataka 11 \n5 Kerala 2 \n6 Madhya Pradesh 12 \n7 Maharashtra 7 \n8 Nagaland 2 \n9 Odisha 32 \n10 Rajasthan 19 \n11 Tamil Nadu 9 \n12 Telangana 44 \n13 Uttar Pradesh 1 \n14 Baseline Geoscience Survey 13 \n  Total 191 \n  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_359": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PLANNING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 359 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nCENTRAL INVESTMENT \n \n†359. SHRI ASHOK KUMAR RAWAT: \n       \n      Will the Minister of PLANNING be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the quantum of central investments made in the country, especially in the backward and \nrural areas as on date during the last three years, year-wise; \n \n(b) the names of the States where the quantum of investments made is lesser than other \nStates; and \n \n(c) the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF PLANNING \nAND MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF \nSTATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) to (c): The information is being collected. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_360": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 360 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nAAROGYA SETU APP \n \n360.     SHRI NATARAJAN P.R.: \n \nWill the Minister of ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY   be \npleased to State: \n \n(a) whether the Aarogya Setu App was created under the PPP mode; \n(b) if so, the details thereof including the terms and conditions of private developers \nrole in the development of the app; and \n(c) the details of the action plan proposed by the Government to leverage the second \napp in view of less number of users of this contract tracing app? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR   ELECTRONICS AND INFORMATION  TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI SANJAY   DHOTRE) \n \n(a):  Yes, Sir. T he Aarogya  Setu App has been developed by National Informatics \nCentre, in partnership with individual volunteers from industry and academia. \n \n(b):    The Individual volunteers from industry and academia made their contributions \nto the App development on a pro-bono basis in an individual capacity. \n \n(c):    Aarogya Setu is the single contact tracing App of Government of India with \nmore than 16 Crore registered Users. This makes Aarogya Setu the largest App based \ncontact tracing platform in the world. \n \n******** \n  \n\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_361": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.361\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021\nSUPPORT ON FARM BILL\n361.    SHRI SYED IMTIAZ JALEEL:\n  SHRI ASADUDDIN OWAISI:\n           \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) whether some countries including PIOs have given support to the\nagitation  of  Indian  farmers  against  three  bills  passed  by  Indian\nParliament;\n(b) if so, the names of the countries where such protest took place and\nstatements issued by some country heads in support of farmers\nagitation;\n(c) whether  the  Government  has  taken  up  the  matter  with  these\ncountries warning them not to interfere in the internal matters of\nIndia; and\n(d)  if so, the details of  the view point of those countries?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS [SHRI V\nMURALEEDHARAN]\n(a) & (b)  No  foreign  government  has  given  support  to  agitation  of\nIndian farmers against three bills passed by Indian Parliament. In Canada,\nUK, USA, and in few European countries, protests by a few motivated PIO’s\non issues related to the Indian Farm Bill have been reported. Canadian PM\nJustin Trudeau made a comment on issues related to farmers in India. \n(c) & (d)  We have taken up this matter with the Canadian authorities\nboth  in  Ottawa  and  New  Delhi  and  conveyed  that  such  comments\npertaining  to  the  internal  affairs  of  the  India  are  unwarranted,\nunacceptable  and  would  damage  India-Canada  bilateral  relations.\nGovernment  of  Canada  has  welcomed  the  Government  of  India’s\ncommitment to ongoing dialogue with the farmers to discuss issues of\nconcern. \n***",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_362": "                     \n \n \n           GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n                                    MINISTRY OF CULTURE \n                                     LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 362 \n  TO BE ANSWERED ON 22.03.2021 \n \n \nRENOVATION OF HISTORICAL BUILDINGS \n \n*362. SHRI UPENDRA SINGH RAWAT: \nSHRI RAMESH BIDHURI: \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of Culture be pleased to state:- \n  \n (a) whether any survey of historically important buildings including   \nmonuments/forts has been conducted and if so, the details thereof, State/UT-\nwise, particularly in Uttar Pradesh, Delhi and Bhagalpur district of Bihar; \n(b) whether most of these buildings/forts/monuments are in  dilapidated condition \nand are in urgent need of repairs and further maintenance;  \n (c) if so, the details of such building/forts/monuments in the country, State/UT-wise  \nand the list of buildings repaired in Uttar Pradesh, Delhi and Bihar during the \nlast three years, year-wise, district-wise and location-wise along with the funds \nallocated and spent thereon; \n (d) whether the Archaeological Survey of India proposes to take over these \nforts/buildings/heritage sites and ensure proper  upkeep and maintenance \nthereof; and \n (e) if so, the details thereof along with the steps taken for the proper maintenance \nof ancient monuments, particularly in Delhi? \n \n \n       ANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR CULTURE & TOURISM \n \n              (SHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL) \n \n \n \n(a)to(e) A statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 362 FOR 22.03.2021 \n \n \n \n(a) Conducting survey/exploration to identify/located ancient sites/ \nmonuments/ building or fort is a regular phenomenon of Archaeological \nSurvey of India. Details of potential monuments/site identified for \ndeclaring them as Centrally protected Monuments/sites is at Annexure.  \n \n(b) No sir, the conservation work of centrally protected monuments in the \ncountry, including Uttar Pradesh, Delhi and Bihar, is attended regularly \nby the Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) according to the need and \nas per the availability of funds and resources, and they are in a good \nstate of preservation. \n \n(c)to(e) There are 743 centrally protected monuments/sites in Uttar Pradesh, \n173 in Delhi and 70 in Bihar. The conservation work of protected \nmonuments/sites is continuous process and it is attended regularly on \nneed basis as per the availability of funds and resources. The details \nof funds allocated and expenditure incurred for conservation and \npreservation of protected monuments in these States are as follows: \n \n                                                                         Amount Rs. in Lakhs \nState Year Funds \nAllocated \nExpenditure \nIncurred \n \nDelhi 2019-20 1542.00 1541.99 \n2018-19 3066.65 3066.00 \n2017-18 3025.00 3025.00 \n   \nUttar \nPradesh \n2019-20 2235.00 2235.00 \n2018-19 1597.00 1595.17 \n2017-18 \n \n1699.00 1698.97 \nBihar 2019-20 195.00 195.00 \n2018-19 176.00 175.98 \n2017-18 155.00 \n \n145.45 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nANNEXURE \n  \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO.362 FOR 22.03.2021 \n \nDETAILS OF MONUMENTS IDENTIFIED FOR DECLARING THEM AS OF NATIONAL \nIMPORTANCE  \n \nSl. \nNo. \nName Of Monuments Locality/District State \n1. Rock Paintings Chintakunta, District   \nY.S.R. Kadapa \nAndhra \nPradesh \n2. Ancient Site Khirsara, District Kacchh Gujarat \n3. Ancient Mounds 6 & 7  Rakhigarhi, District Hisar Haryana \n4. Kaleshwar Mahadev \nTemple   \nKalesar, District  Kangra Himachal \nPradesh \n5. Terracotta Brick Temples Doisa Nagar, \nNavratangarh, Sisai, \nDistrict Gumla \nJharkhand \n6. Rock Paintings Isko, District Hazaribagh Jharkhand \n7. Rock Art Site Murgi  Rdanag, District Leh Ladakh -   UT \n8. Ancient Caves Saspol / \nGon-Nila-Phuk Medition \ncaves    \nSaspol, District Leh Ladakh -   UT \n9. Ancient Buddhist institute \nremains \nNyarma, District Leh Ladakh -   UT \n10. Tirisha Stupa along with \nadjoining remains and \nprehistoric site around holy \nlake \nDistrict Leh Ladakh -   UT \n11. Ancient Khar (Castle)  Scurbuchan, District Leh Ladakh -   UT \n12. Ancient Menhirs  Lungphunlian, \nDistrict Champhai   \nMizoram \n13. Ancient Menhirs and \nSettlement \nDungtlang, \nDistrict Champhai \nMizoram \n14. Ancient Menhirs and Rock \nEngraving  \nFarkawan,   \nDistrict Champhai \nMizoram \n15. Archaeological sites and \nremains \nMasol, District Mohali Punjab \n16. Ancient Naula  Village Syunrakat, District \nAlmora   \nUttarakhand \n17. Four temples located \nadjacent to the Centrally \nprotected monument \nKuber Temples \nDistrict Almora Uttarakhand \n18. Archaeological Site, Talab \nTank and Baoli  \nGanesh   Bagh,  \nDistrict Chitrakut  \nUttar Pradesh \n19. Nakkar Khana Lucknow Uttar Pradesh \n20. Archaeological site  Sisvania, District Basti   Uttar Pradesh \n21. Group of Rock Paintings Fatehpur Sikri, District \nAgra \nUttar Pradesh \n \n \n******* ",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_363": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 363\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021\nDAM ON BRAHMAPUTRA\n†363. DR. DEEPAK BAIJ:\nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) whether China is working on a proposal for constructing a big dam almost\nthirty Kilometers before Indian border on Brahmaputra river in Tibet and if\nso, the details thereof;\n(b) whether an assessment of loss in Indian region in future has been made in\nview of the water capacity of the dam and if so, the details thereof;\n(c) whether the said dam is a threat to India in the opinion of experts; and\n(d) if so, the details of the steps to be taken to check the likely loss to India\ndue to sudden release of water from the said dam proposed by China?\n \nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n(SHRI V. MURALEEDHARAN)\n(a) to (d) Government has taken note of reports regarding China’s plans for\nhydropower development on the lower reaches of the Brahmaputra river.\nGovernment  carefully  monitors  all  developments  on  the  Brahmaputra\nriver. As a lower riparian state, with considerable established user rights to the\nwaters  of  the  trans-border  rivers,  Government has  consistently  conveyed its\nviews and concerns to the Chinese authorities and has urged them to ensure that\nthe interests of downstream States are not harmed by any activities in upstream\nareas. The Chinese side has conveyed to us on several occasions that they are\nonly  undertaking  run-of-the-river  hydropower  projects,  which  do  not  involve\ndiversion of the waters of the Brahmaputra. \nVarious  issues  relating to  trans-border  rivers  are  discussed  with China\nunder  the  ambit  of  an  institutionalized  Expert  Level  Mechanism  which  was\nestablished in 2006, as well as through diplomatic channels. We intend to remain\nengaged with China on the issue of trans-border rivers to safeguard our interests.\n***",
    "ls|LS17_S5_U_364": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.364 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021 \n \nRAIL LAND DEVELOPMENT AUTHORITY \n \n364. SHRI ABDUL KHALEQUE: \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of the revenue earned through auctioning of land by \nRail Land Development Authority during the last three years; \n \n(b) the locations where Rail Land Development Authority has \nidentified land for auctioning in the next three years and the \nestimated value; and \n \n(c) whether any location from Assam features in the list particularly \nin the districts of Bongaigaon, Barpeta, Nalbari and Chirang and \nif so, the details thereof? \n \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMERCE & INDUSTRY AND \n CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD & PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION  \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n(a) Rail Land Development Authority (RLDA) leases the land \nthrough open competitive bidding process.  \n \n…2/- \n \n\n \n-2- \nThe revenue earned by RLDA during last three years is as follows:- \nYear Revenue earned \n( ` in Cr) \n2017-18 42.93 \n2018-19 82.81 \n2019-20 933.27 \n \n(b) RLDA has been entrusted with 84 sites, out of which 26 sites \nhave been bid out till now. The remaining sites which have earning \npotential of approximately `6500 Cr. are identified for bidding during \nnext two to three years. \n \n(c) No, Sir. \n \n***** ",
