    "ls|LS17_S5_U_383": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.383\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2021\nPOPSK IN DISTRICTS\n383.  DR. SUJAY RADHAKRISHNA VIKHE PATIL:\nDR. HEENA GAVIT:\nDR. SHRIKANT EKNATH SHINDE:\nSHRI HEMANT SRIRAM PATIL:\nSHRI UNMESH BHAIYYASAHEB PATIL:\nSHRI DHAIRYASHEEL SAMBHAJIRAO MANE:\nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state:\n(a) whether there is any proposal to start Post Office Passport Seva\nKendras (POPSKs) in all district headquarters or in all Parliamentary\nconstituencies;\n(b) if so, the details thereof and the number of POPSKs set up so far;\n(c) the  number  of  POPSKs  which  have  started  functioning  so  far  in\nMaharashtra along with the number of POPSKs proposed to be made\noperational in the near future; and\n(d) the extent to which getting passports is likely to become easier\nthrough POPSKs along with the details of its style of functioning?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR EXTERNAL AFFAIRS\n[SHRI V. MURALEEDHARAN]\n(a) The Ministry, in association with the Department of Posts, decided in\nJanuary 2017 to open Passport Kendras at the Head Post Offices (HPO)/\nPost Offices (PO) in the country called ‘Post Office Passport Seva Kendra’\n(POPSK) in each Parliamentary constituency where there is no Passport\nSeva Kendra (PSK).\n(b) The  list  of  426  functional  POPSKs  in  the  country  is  placed  at\nAnnexure-I. \n(c) Out of 48 Parliamentary (Lok Sabha) Constituencies in Maharashtra,\nthere  are  37  POPSKs  and  8  Passport  Seva  Kendras  covering  44\nParliamentary  Constituencies.  The  Ministry  is  working  with  the\nDepartment  of  Posts  to  operationalize  POPSKs  at  remaining  four  Lok\nSabha Constituencies. \n(d) The Ministry has eased the passport issuing process and has made it\nan  online  procedure  including  getting  appointments  for  submission  of\ndocuments for passports. Effective technical infrastructure is in place to\nensure that the Passport Seva system is available for access at all times\nfrom  any  location.  The  Passport  Portal  (www.passportindia.gov.in)  is\naccessible to anyone, anywhere and anytime. With a view to address the\nchallenge of digital divide, especially in the rural hinterland, the Ministry in\nassociation with Common Service Centres e-Governance Services India\n1\n\nLtd. (which is promoted by the Department of Electronics and IT), has\nfacilitated online filing of passport applications, through the vast network\nof CSCs across rural hinterland.\nPost  Office  Passport  Seva  Kendras  (POPSK)  are  being  set  up  in\nassociation  with  the  Department  of  Posts  in  order  to  bring  passport\nservices closer to people  residing in villages/remote/rural areas of the\ncountry.  Applicants,  who  apply  for  their  passports  online  through  the\npassport  portal,  can  schedule  an  appointment  and  then  visit  the\ndesignated POPSK to complete the formalities, prior to the issue of the\npassport.  The  photographs,  biometrics  and  the  supporting  documents\nwould be electronically captured at the POPSK prior to the issue of the\nPassport.\nOpening  of  POPSK  has  facilitated  the  Ministry  in  taking\npassport services closer to the citizens of the country.\n***\n2\n\nAnnexure- I to Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 383\nList of functional Post Office Passport Seva Kendras\nS.No. Locations State/UT Passport Office\n1 Port Blair Andaman & Nicobar Island Kolkata\n2 Anantapur Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n3 Bapatla Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n4 Chittoor Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n5 Gudivada Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n6 Guntur Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n7 Hindupur Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n8 Kadapa Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n9 Kodur Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n10 Kurnool Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n11 Nandyal Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n12 Narasaraopet Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n13 Nellore Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n14 Ongole Andhra Pradesh Vijayawada\n15 Amalapuram Andhra 